<p><em>PM request acknowledged.</em></p>
<hr />
<p>T.L. at your service!</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Here&nbsp;lies&nbsp;crit&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Bye&nbsp;bye&nbsp;crit&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>it is an eldritch being that cannot comprehend whose proper form</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What did you mean by this? It can't comprehend who's proper form? Could you maybe clarify this?</p>
<p>I personally think the general appearance of the entity and aspects of the entity itself is quite cliche; it makes me think of other SCPs and other spooky humanoids like Look-See, Slenderman, SCP-106, and many others I can’t remember the names of. Adding on, the major world disasters because of an entity’s instability is majorly overdone. However, I am way more concerned about your narrative portion. Is there a reason behind why it is being referred to as a bartender? Just wearing a bartender suit only constitutes a fraction of being a bartender, or it might not at all. I don’t really see such a huge connection with this aspect and the rest of the narrative. Does it actually have anything to do with it? What’s the full history behind this entity? What made it the way it is now? Where did the theories of its existence come from? How did it end up at the Foundation? If it can talk, why not have the Foundation conduct interviews with it? Could you maybe do into detail with its anomalous abilities? Honestly, what you have as a narrative isn’t really considered a narrative. It’s just a series of more information/suggestions of more information about the entity’s abilities. You’re going to need a better plot for this concept to work out, and I either recommend fleshing the one you currently have out more or coming up with an even better plot for this instead.</p>
<p>Overall, this is just a bunch of cliches all haphazardly bunched up into a not fully thought out concept. For now, I’d just recommend doing some rework on the narrative to see if this concept might have a fighting chance. Personally, I don’t see this as something successful as of current. But perhaps you can change my mind?</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<br />
If you have any questions regarding my critique, please let me know. You are welcome to PM me for another look, or you may follow up with someone from the Butterfly Squad Roster or IRC Chat rooms.
